<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/4th-century">4th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">325 CE</h1><p class="ref-lede">325 CE in world history: 4 events, 1 birth and 1 death. 142 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/306">306 CE</a><a href="/years/313">313 CE</a><a href="/years/314">314 CE</a><a href="/years/324">324 CE</a><a href="/years/325" aria-current="page">325 CE</a><a href="/years/328">328 CE</a><a href="/years/337">337 CE</a><a href="/years/351">351 CE</a><a href="/years/357">357 CE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/may-20">20 May</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Council of Nicaea opens under Constantine</h3><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">Bishops</a> from across the empire gathered at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicaea">Nicaea</a> in the first ecumenical council of the Church. It condemned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arianism">Arianism</a> and produced the first version of the Nicene Creed.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/first-council-of-nicaea" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/first-council-of-nicaea.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/june-19">19 June</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Bishops at the First Council of Nicaea adopt the Nicene Creed</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-council-of-nicaea">First Council of Nicaea</a>, convened by the emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-i">Constantine I</a>, adopted the original Nicene Creed, whose text ends with anathemas against Arian propositions. According to the traditional view, the creed was amended in 381 at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-council-of-nicaea">First Council of Nicaea</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantine-i">Constantine I</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arianism">Arian</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-25">25 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The First Council of Nicaea closes</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">By tradition the council summoned by Constantine ended on this date. It had condemned <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arianism">Arianism</a>, adopted the Nicene Creed and set rules for dating Easter, shaping Christian doctrine for centuries.</p></div></li></ol></section>
